1
00:00:00,180 --> 00:00:03,373
You want to put AI to work.

2
00:00:03,450 --> 00:00:06,653
But can it access the wrong information?

3
00:00:06,750 --> 00:00:09,450
Are the right protections in place?

4
00:00:09,550 --> 00:00:12,231
And who fixes what is missing?

5
00:00:12,317 --> 00:00:17,645
Meet AI Flight Deck—an orchestration tool for Copilot readiness and rollout.

6
00:00:18,317 --> 00:00:23,261
It brings together visibility, clear next actions, and evidence of progress.

7
00:00:23,350 --> 00:00:25,204
Not just another assessment.

8
00:00:25,650 --> 00:00:31,097
Connect your organisation, review the read permissions, and define your pilot group.

9
00:00:33,150 --> 00:00:36,742
Flight Deck brings the findings into one workspace.

10
00:00:37,850 --> 00:00:39,842
Explore thirteen readiness domains.

11
00:00:40,850 --> 00:00:47,803
See what needs attention, what needs an owner’s review, and what the tool cannot yet verify.

12
00:00:47,883 --> 00:00:51,080
Here, an identity protection check needs attention.

13
00:00:51,150 --> 00:00:54,900
Record the scope, responsible owner and approval reference.

14
00:00:57,150 --> 00:01:02,223
Follow the guidance, with changes made through your normal administration process.

15
00:01:02,317 --> 00:01:04,791
Now report the work complete.

16
00:01:04,883 --> 00:01:06,265
Is it resolved?

17
00:01:06,350 --> 00:01:07,325
Not yet.

18
00:01:08,250 --> 00:01:11,055
A completed task is not proof.

19
00:01:11,150 --> 00:01:15,635
Collect fresh evidence: this supported configuration check is now verified.

20
00:01:18,450 --> 00:01:20,725
Come back and check again.

21
00:01:20,817 --> 00:01:25,559
If later evidence no longer supports the result, the action reopens.

22
00:01:25,650 --> 00:01:29,763
Progress stays connected to evidence—not yesterday’s tick box.

23
00:01:29,850 --> 00:01:33,111
Governance reviews stay distinct from technical checks.

24
00:01:35,350 --> 00:01:40,903
The decision snapshot brings together recorded owners, supporting evidence and remaining blockers.

25
00:01:41,350 --> 00:01:43,155
Start with a pilot.

26
00:01:43,250 --> 00:01:47,917
As rollout expands, repeat the cycle: understand, act, verify, decide.

27
00:01:48,017 --> 00:01:51,567
AI Flight Deck—do not just assess readiness.

28
00:01:51,650 --> 00:01:56,203
Orchestrate the next steps, and move forward with evidence.
